{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>As the deer</b> — The matter of the deer that eats snakes and its innards grow hot is well known; then it seeks strong streams of water." "<b>And 'ayal</b> — in the feminine, like: <i>'ez bat shenahta</i> (a sturdy she-goat of your flock)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {1 "The cited phrase appears to echo the idiom in Proverbs 5:19, 'אילת אהבים ויעלת חן'; the precise citation and its bearing on the feminine gender of איל is somewhat obscure."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:33.696014364Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}